        <name>Languages</name>
        <qualifiedname>FTryllModelManifestEntry::Languages</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>BCP-47 primary language subtags this model declares, cached from the catalog.</para>
<para>The one piece of catalog metadata cached here rather than read live. Everything else can wait for a ListModels round trip, but the settings language dropdown and the model-picker warnings have to work with no server running - an editor that can only validate languages while connected would be worse than no validation at all. Written by the Model Manager from the live <ref refid="struct_f_tryll_model_info" kindref="compound">FTryllModelInfo</ref> at the moment the model is registered.</para>
<para>Empty means undeclared, not &quot;supports nothing&quot;. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
